{%- comment -%}
  How a custom order runs, start to finish. Brief §9.4.

  Five steps, and the reason this section exists at all is that a B2B enquiry is
  a commitment with no visible price. A shopper buying trousers knows exactly
  what happens next; an organisation asking about 200 uniforms does not, and the
  thing that stops them asking is not knowing how much process they are about to
  sign up for. So the section's job is to make the process look finite.

  THE NUMBER IS DERIVED FROM BLOCK ORDER, never typed into a setting. A step
  numbered by hand goes wrong the first time somebody inserts a step in the
  middle — the studio would have to renumber every block after it, and the one
  they miss is the one that ships. Reordering blocks in the theme editor
  renumbers the whole row here.

  It is zero-padded to two digits, which is the brief's own notation ("01 —
  Consultation"). Liquid has no pad filter, so ten or more steps would need a
  second branch; the guard below covers it rather than silently rendering "010".

  THE NUMBER IS SET IN THE BRAND COLOUR, not in a hairline tint. A process step's
  number is content — it says which step this is and in what order — so it has to
  be readable, and the editorial move of setting big numerals in near-invisible
  grey would make the one piece of ordering information on the page the hardest
  thing on it to read. The rule that colour never carries meaning alone applies
  to legibility too.

  The top rule on each cell is what reads as a process bar at `lg`, where the
  five cells sit in a row. Below that they stack and each rule becomes a plain
  divider, which is the same thing doing a smaller job.
{%- endcomment -%}

<section aria-labelledby="how-it-works-heading" class="border-y border-rule bg-canvas">
  <div class="mx-auto w-full max-w-content px-gutter py-section">
    <div data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-4">
      <h2 id="how-it-works-heading" class="text-h1 leading-h1">
        {% render 'copy', value: section.settings.heading, label: 'heading' %}
      </h2>

      {%- if section.settings.body != blank -%}
        <p class="wl-measure text-body leading-body text-ink-muted">{{ section.settings.body }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>

    <ol class="mt-block grid gap-7 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-5">
      {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign step = forloop.index
          if step < 10
            assign step_label = step | prepend: '0'
          else
            assign step_label = step | append: ''
          endif
        -%}
        <li data-reveal class="flex flex-col gap-2.5 border-t border-line pt-5" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
          <span class="font-display text-h1 leading-none text-brand">{{ step_label }}</span>

          <h3 class="text-h3 leading-h3 font-medium text-ink">
            {% render 'copy', value: block.settings.title, label: 'step', inline: true %}
          </h3>

          <p class="text-caption leading-snug text-ink-muted">
            {% render 'copy', value: block.settings.body, label: 'detail', lines: 2 %}
          </p>
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "How it works",
  "max_blocks": 8,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Steps are numbered from their order here — do not type a number into the name. Reorder the blocks and the numbering follows." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "How it works" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Intro" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "step",
      "name": "Step",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Name" },
        { "type": "textarea", "id": "body", "label": "Detail" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "How it works",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "step", "settings": { "title": "Consultation", "body": "You tell us what the organisation needs." } },
        { "type": "step", "settings": { "title": "Product & specification", "body": "Model, material, colour, size, branding and product detail are settled." } },
        { "type": "step", "settings": { "title": "Quotation", "body": "Wear Label prices the order against that specification and the quantity." } },
        { "type": "step", "settings": { "title": "Production", "body": "Sample, approval, then the production run." } },
        { "type": "step", "settings": { "title": "Delivery", "body": "Finished pieces are shipped to you." } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
